  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "While the estimation of genotype means for a candidate locus seems straightforward, there are several potential sources of bias. While it is possible in some settings to distinguish between the direct effects of a candidate locus and its indirect effects due to association with linked QTLs (e.g., Bovenhuis and Weller 1994), as noted above the presence of linkage disequilibrium greatly confounds the interpretation of candidate-locus means. We consider other, more subtle, sources of bias below.",
      "source_page": 436,
      "printed_page": 416,
